<title>JAPAN: Tokyo precious metals market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Tokyo precious metals market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The yen-based Tokyo precious metals futures market is closed for a national holiday on Monday. Trading will resume on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On Friday, precious metals futures ended firmer.</p>
<p>TOCOM most-active benchmark December gold ended nine yen per gram higher at 1,344 yen, while bullion was quoted at $369.15/45 per ounce at the Tokyo close.</p>
</text>
